extraction_notes: |
  - The book names this an R.C.C. (printed 74, "Psi-Tech R.C.C."; stat block printed 76 "Psi-Tech Psychic R.C.C."); per the Psyscape batch convention it is stored as category occ, occ_group psychic, modelled on mind-melter. men_of_arms false: it sits in the book''s psychic R.C.C. section, not a Men of Arms heading.
  - xp_table taken from the batch brief (read off the printed 157 table).
  - Race: not a distinct race. Printed 76 says most are human (80%), with Elves (6%), Ogres (6%) and 8% others; male or female. No race_restrictions stored.
  - Attribute requirement I.Q. 10 (printed 76); high M.E. and P.P. are helpful only. Alignment: any.
  - Psionics (printed 75, items 1 and 5): Telemechanics is granted by name and its always-on, no-I.S.P., doubled-duration, 85% +1%/level form is described in special_abilities. Automatic powers Telemechanic Mental Operation, Telemechanic Paralysis, Telemechanic Possession, Machine Ghost, Object Read, Speed Reading and Total Recall; "Object Read" is the catalog row Object Read (Psychometry). Two Sensitive picks at level one (powers_starting 2). "At each subsequent level" one pick from Physical or Sensitive (levels 2-15); one Super pick at levels 2, 4, 8 and 12 as printed. Master Psychic: saves vs psionics on 10 or higher (implied by type master).
  - I.S.P. (printed 76, item 6): cache reads "6.1.S.P.: 3D4xlO"; stored as 3D4x10 + M.E., +10 per level. P.P.E. 1D6+2 (item 7).
  - Bonuses (printed 76, item 8): only +1 save vs possession is unconditional and stored. +5 vs Horror Factor (machines involved) and +2 initiative (against machines) are conditional and live in special_abilities, as do all Mental Link bonuses (printed 75, item 4), which apply only while piloting.
  - Machine & Electrical Diagnosis (6 I.S.P.) is a class ability, not a catalog psionic row; stored as a special ability, not in powers.
  - Skills: bases are catalog base + printed bonus. Basic Math -> Mathematics: Basic. "Literacy: American" -> Literacy: Native Language (the catalog has no American literacy row); the second literacy is Literacy: Other. "Read Sensory Equipment" -> catalog Sensory Equipment (Pilot Related). No native spoken language is printed; two Language: Other picks are stored as the sibling Psyscape drafts do.
  - Hand to Hand (printed 76): no style is granted; it must be bought as a related skill - Basic 1, Expert 2, Martial Arts 3 (hand_to_hand costs). No Assassin option printed.
  - Related skills: five at level one, two more at levels 2, 4, 7, 10 and 13. Military "any involving machines, building & demolitions" is a judgement call: demolitions, armorer/weapon-making, fortification, traps and space defense systems. Science "Chemistry and Math only": Chemistry and Mathematics: Advanced (Mathematics: Basic is already an R.C.C. skill; the other chemistry specialties were left out). Physical excludes Acrobatics, Wrestling and Boxing.
  - Secondary skills: four at level one, two more at levels 2, 4, 6, 9, 12 and 15, as printed.
  - Equipment (printed 76): "several sets of utility clothes" stored as clothing x3 (a judgement on "several"). Work coveralls -> coveralls-work; steel-toed work boots -> steel-toe-boots; light M.D.C. armor -> light-mdc-body-armor (its "one special feature of the player''s choice" modification is not stored). Extensive tool kit -> large-tool-kit; smaller portable tool kit -> portable-tool-kit; measuring tape -> conventional-tape-measure; half dozen flares -> flare x6; 200 ft lightweight rope -> lightweight-rope; "a couple knives" -> knife x2; hammer -> hammer-tool.
  - Equipment NOT stored (no catalog row found): 1D4 rolls of electrical tape, notebook, reinforced padded briefcase (10 M.D.C.), large wrench, personal items and basic tools of the trade, and 4D6 spare gadgets, parts and components (circuit boards, motors, drive train, robot arm, etc.).
  - Vehicle: a souped-up hover cycle or Land Rover with 10% more M.D.C. and 10% more speed. The catalog has no Land Rover; jeep stands in. The +10% is not stored.
  - Money (printed 76): 4D6x100 credits stored; the further 4D4x1000 credits worth of tools, spare parts and components cannot be held by starting_money and is recorded here.
  - Cybernetics: starts with none; avoids them except for medical reasons (stored as a restriction line).
---

## Lore

Psi-Techs are psychics born with an intuitive grasp of machinery, able to operate, repair, improvise and build almost any device, and to reach into computers undetected through Machine Ghost. Where an ordinary mechanic must strip a machine down or run diagnostics, a Psi-Tech senses the fault with his mind and knows at once how to fix it, even for alien machines and Techno-Wizard devices. That makes them sought after by industry, scientists, criminal organisations and, by rumour, the Coalition''s own research into lost and alien technology. The flip side is that many are shy, awkward and easily intimidated around people, preferring the company of other Psi-Techs, robots and machines.

## GM Notes

**The repressed alter ego.** A small minority of Psi-Techs harbour a reckless, sometimes vengeful or even murderous second personality that surfaces only when they are in control of a powerful machine - piloting power armor, a giant robot or a robot vehicle. The book stresses such cases are rare. Not modelled; use it as a roleplaying hook.

**Soup-Up Machines in play.** The 10%/15% improvements and the doubled work speed are narrative; the sheet does not alter vehicle or weapon stats. The starting vehicle is already souped up (+10% M.D.C. and speed), which the equipment list cannot show.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'psi-tech');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'psi-tech';

